{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For six days YHWH made.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): its sense is 'in the six' (בששת), and like it (Genesis 14:4): ״ושלש עשרה שנה מרדו״." "<b>And by way of</b> reason (sekhel): 'six days YHWH made' — and included within this is creation itself, for they (the days) are included therein (in the act of making); and this demonstrates that time was created, for had it said 'in six days' (בששת ימים) it would have indicated that time was preexistent." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'for six days' is the time of the standing of the world in its settlement, and the drawing forth of the supernal heavens and earth from above, and their flow into the heavens and earth below, and this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:33.599846660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}